WEBVTT

00:04.815 --> 00:07.613
&lt;i>Bill, did you notice
that girl coming down the slope?&lt;/i>

00:07.784 --> 00:10.150
You might wanna eat
so that when you throw up...

00:10.320 --> 00:13.653
...it won't just be alcohol
and stomach juice.

00:14.591 --> 00:19.494
Way ahead of you.
I call it an Egg McBourbon.

00:21.231 --> 00:22.459
So this is your life now?

00:22.633 --> 00:25.864
You just sit here miserable and alone,
waiting for Chelsea to call.

00:26.036 --> 00:29.005
I'm not waiting for her to call.
I'm watching TV.

00:29.172 --> 00:31.663
And, occasionally, I cry.

00:32.342 --> 00:35.539
You do realize you're watching
The Weather Channel?

00:37.848 --> 00:41.045
- Happy?
- Oh, yeah, The Pet Channel.

00:41.251 --> 00:45.017
Who doesn't enjoy seeing a dog
get his anal glands expressed?

00:47.624 --> 00:49.319
Chelsea?

00:50.727 --> 00:52.524
- Your ex-wife.
- Oh.

00:52.696 --> 00:55.028
Speaking of having
one's anal glands expressed.

00:56.233 --> 00:57.928
Hi, Judith, what's up?

00:58.101 --> 01:00.433
Oh. Oh, I'm so sorry. That's terrible.

01:01.505 --> 01:04.804
Her grandfather died.
He was 94. It's no big deal.

01:06.176 --> 01:08.337
Well, he's in a better place now.

01:08.512 --> 01:11.345
He has to be. He lived in Sacramento.

01:12.349 --> 01:13.941
I'm sorry, what's that?

01:14.418 --> 01:15.942
You're kidding.

01:16.119 --> 01:18.553
Oh. Oh, I always loved that clock.

01:18.722 --> 01:20.917
He left me his grandfather clock.

01:21.091 --> 01:24.117
Very old, worth a fortune.
I can sell it and buy a new car.

01:24.294 --> 01:26.785
Oh, Judith, that's just tragic.

01:26.964 --> 01:30.092
So, uh, when are they gonna
deliver the clock?

01:30.267 --> 01:31.291
Oh, yeah.

01:31.468 --> 01:35.700
Yeah, I guess your grandmother does
have more important things to box up.

01:36.440 --> 01:37.907
Like your grandfather.

01:40.043 --> 01:42.944
You're right, not funny.
She never got my sense of humor.

01:44.147 --> 01:47.548
Uh, well, I guess I'll just drive up
to Sacramento and pick it up.

01:47.718 --> 01:50.744
Uh, well,
once again, my deepest sympathies.

01:50.921 --> 01:52.548
Okay.

01:53.490 --> 01:55.424
Score.

01:56.827 --> 01:57.885
Help me out here.

01:58.061 --> 02:00.928
Why would Judith's grandfather
leave you a valuable antique?

02:01.098 --> 02:03.362
He liked me. I was the only one
who would sit for hours...

02:03.533 --> 02:05.558
...listening to his stories about Korea.

02:05.969 --> 02:08.460
- He fought in Korea?
- No, he was a sex tourist.

02:09.973 --> 02:11.270
Very creepy.

02:11.441 --> 02:13.932
You know,
I always admired that clock.

02:14.111 --> 02:17.808
I remember the first time I saw it, I said,
"Bill, that is a hell of a clock."

02:17.981 --> 02:21.940
Uh, and he was hard of hearing,
so that led to the Korea stories.

02:22.953 --> 02:25.581
Oh, hey, you wanna drive up
and get it with me?

02:25.756 --> 02:28.316
Let's see, do I wanna drive six hours
to Sacramento...

02:28.492 --> 02:31.427
...to pick up a dead guy's clock?

02:31.628 --> 02:32.959
With me.

02:34.498 --> 02:36.022
Don't take this the wrong way...

02:36.233 --> 02:39.225
...but I would rather
get a maple-syrup enema...

02:40.270 --> 02:43.433
...and then sit on an anthill.

02:46.143 --> 02:47.542
You didn't just make that up.

02:47.744 --> 02:50.611
No, I've actually compiled a list
of things I'd rather do...

02:50.781 --> 02:53.944
...than spend long periods of time
with you in an enclosed space.

02:54.818 --> 02:56.308
- You wanna hear some more?
- No.

02:56.486 --> 03:00.513
You sure? I got a beauty that involves
hemorrhoids, a bottlebrush and sea salt.

03:01.191 --> 03:04.058
- No, I get it. I'll just take Jake.
- Wait, wait, wait.

03:04.261 --> 03:06.195
So both you and Jake
are gonna be going?

03:06.363 --> 03:09.355
- Yes.
- Score.

03:13.870 --> 03:17.328
&lt;i>Here's ordinary cat litter
after five days of continuous use...&lt;/i>

03:17.507 --> 03:19.634
&lt;i>... by a relatively healthy cat.&lt;/i>

03:19.810 --> 03:23.246
&lt;i>Yuck! Looks bad, smells worse.&lt;/i>

03:23.413 --> 03:27.543
&lt;i>Now here's Magic Pussy Litter
with its patented Cluster Busters.&lt;/i>

03:27.718 --> 03:31.313
Oh, that is really cool.

03:32.089 --> 03:34.387
- Hey.
- Hey.

03:34.558 --> 03:36.822
- What you watching?
- An amazing breakthrough...

03:36.993 --> 03:39.689
...in cat-crap technology.

03:39.863 --> 03:43.390
Dad says you're vegging in front
of the TV because you still miss Chelsea.

03:43.567 --> 03:48.664
- Well, he's right, for a change.
- You know, I kind of do too.

03:48.839 --> 03:52.331
Remember how she would lean over
to pour cereal for breakfast...

03:52.509 --> 03:54.443
...and you could see
right down her robe?

03:56.747 --> 03:58.738
Too soon?

04:01.418 --> 04:02.885
What are you doing up so late?

04:03.053 --> 04:05.385
I was hungry.
Wanna join me for a grilled cheese?

04:05.555 --> 04:07.853
- No.
- Pigs in a blanket?

04:08.024 --> 04:09.082
I'm all right.

04:09.259 --> 04:12.524
- Two ice-cream sandwiches on a waffle?
- I'll pass.

04:13.063 --> 04:15.623
It's no trouble.
I'm making them anyway.

04:16.266 --> 04:18.200
I'm fine.

04:19.836 --> 04:22.202
You know, I really am sorry
about you and Chelsea.

04:22.372 --> 04:24.863
Well, thanks, buddy.

04:27.077 --> 04:28.544
Her boobs are real, right?

04:31.214 --> 04:33.273
- Yep.
- Outstanding.

05:07.317 --> 05:10.753
- When can I drive?
- When I get tired.

05:10.921 --> 05:13.549
Relax, take in the scenery.

05:14.090 --> 05:16.183
Okay, now what?

05:16.860 --> 05:18.350
I don't know, um...

05:18.562 --> 05:22.498
- We enjoy each other's company.
- All right.

05:34.878 --> 05:36.846
Okay, now what?

05:37.480 --> 05:40.176
This is a golden opportunity
to get to know each other...

05:40.350 --> 05:42.113
...as more than just father and son.

05:42.619 --> 05:43.711
What else are we?

05:43.887 --> 05:47.823
We're two men on the open road,
free and unencumbered.

05:48.191 --> 05:51.160
Oh. What's unencumbered?

05:51.661 --> 05:55.119
Uh, no restraints.
We can do whatever we want. Ha, ha.

05:55.298 --> 05:56.526
Okay.

05:56.700 --> 05:58.224
I wanna drive.

05:58.401 --> 06:00.392
Later. Pick something else.

06:05.709 --> 06:07.870
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Oh! Oh.

06:08.044 --> 06:09.807
- Yeah.
- Oh!

06:09.980 --> 06:12.210
Oh, well, very funny.

06:12.382 --> 06:14.782
So you wanna go toot for toot?
Well, check this out.

06:17.687 --> 06:19.621
- Wow. Ha, ha.
- Mm-hm. Mm-hm.

06:19.789 --> 06:23.247
That is a bran muffin
and a half a grapefruit, my friend.

06:23.426 --> 06:26.054
This is a grilled-cheese sandwich,
pigs in a blanket...

06:26.229 --> 06:27.821
...and a waffle ice-cream sandwich.

06:29.199 --> 06:30.894
- Ha, ha.
- Oh. Oh, yeah? Oh, yeah?

06:31.067 --> 06:33.194
Well, this is an antidepressant
and a mochaccino.

06:42.679 --> 06:43.805
Uh-oh.

06:44.848 --> 06:47.282
Keep an eye out for a gas station.

06:50.720 --> 06:53.518
Twenty-eight, 29, 30.

06:53.690 --> 06:56.716
Oh, hell, she ain't gonna miss one.

06:58.028 --> 07:00.053
- Hey, Russell.
- Oh, hey, Charlie.

07:00.230 --> 07:01.720
You want a muscle relaxer?

07:01.898 --> 07:03.297
You take one with Viagra...

07:03.466 --> 07:06.094
...and you're essentially Gumby
with a Pokey.

07:08.204 --> 07:09.398
No, thanks.

07:09.572 --> 07:11.938
I actually have a prescription
from a doctor.

07:12.108 --> 07:17.444
Whoa, look at you,
following the letter and spirit of the law.

07:19.249 --> 07:21.376
Sleeping pills. Those can be fun.

07:21.551 --> 07:24.987
You know, with a couple Red Bulls
so you don't fall asleep.

07:25.488 --> 07:28.218
The party is over, Russell.
I need to get some sleep.

07:28.391 --> 07:31.451
Ah. Well, then you don't want this. No.

07:31.628 --> 07:35.325
You want something organic,
something created by Mother Nature.

07:35.498 --> 07:38.228
- What do you got in mind?
- Ganja.

07:39.803 --> 07:42.567
- You trying to sell me pot?
- Ah, not just pot.

07:42.739 --> 07:45.765
I call this Ojai Sohigh. Heh.

07:45.942 --> 07:50.436
Two hits and a couple chicken burritos
and it's "Good night, Irene."

07:51.147 --> 07:54.412
- Don't you need a prescription for that?
- What are you, a cop?

07:56.019 --> 07:59.216
Okay, okay,
but you're just driving the price up.

08:00.757 --> 08:04.523
&lt;i>- Hello?
- Dr. Gollygupta, Russell here.&lt;/i>

08:04.728 --> 08:07.720
&lt;i>Oh, hello, Russell.
How are they hanging?&lt;/i>

08:07.897 --> 08:11.355
Twice the length of my penis,
thanks for asking.

08:11.534 --> 08:14.970
&lt;i>- My friend here needs a prescription.
- All right, uh, let me see him.&lt;/i>

08:15.138 --> 08:16.366
Oh, okay.

08:16.539 --> 08:19.030
Charlie, I'd like you
to meet Dr. Gollygupta...

08:19.242 --> 08:23.474
...of the Gollygupta Hypertension
and Glaucoma Clinic in Sri Lanka.

08:23.646 --> 08:25.841
&lt;i>Please to turn your head and cough.&lt;/i>

08:26.016 --> 08:27.711
Just turn like that. Yeah, and:

08:29.119 --> 08:31.383
&lt;i>- There you go.
- Oh, that's no good.&lt;/i>

08:33.390 --> 08:35.756
&lt;i>I'll send you prescription.&lt;/i>

08:38.228 --> 08:40.025
&lt;i>Excuse me.&lt;/i>

08:42.766 --> 08:46.202
&lt;i>Hello, Direc TV Customer Service...&lt;/i>

08:46.369 --> 08:48.030
&lt;i>... Roger speaking.&lt;/i>

08:50.640 --> 08:52.039
Here it is.

08:52.709 --> 08:55.007
Ah-ha! Great news, Charlie.

08:55.178 --> 08:57.078
You've got glaucoma.

08:59.783 --> 09:04.015
You know, for gas-station sweatpants,
these aren't bad.

09:04.187 --> 09:06.314
I beg to differ.

09:08.591 --> 09:11.219
May I say that you have become
a very good driver?

09:11.728 --> 09:13.286
"Grand Theft Auto," Dad.

09:13.496 --> 09:16.021
It's like driver's ed,
but with pimps and ho's.

09:16.599 --> 09:18.863
Well, whatever.

09:19.536 --> 09:22.232
So, uh, have you
given any more thought...

09:22.405 --> 09:24.839
...to what you wanna do
after high school?

09:25.008 --> 09:27.806
If this is the college talk,
we need to both be realistic.

09:27.977 --> 09:32.107
Hey, I know a big university is probably
out of reach for the time being...

09:32.315 --> 09:36.581
...but there's still junior colleges,
community colleges, trade schools.

09:37.020 --> 09:40.615
Man, I'd like to trade schools right now
because this one's kicking my ass.

09:41.224 --> 09:43.454
Come on, Jake,
you know what I'm talking about.

09:43.626 --> 09:46.254
- You have to start making plans.
- Did you have plans...

09:46.429 --> 09:48.556
...when you were my age?
- Yeah, I had big plans.

09:48.731 --> 09:50.824
What happened to them?

09:53.336 --> 09:55.133
Just drive.

10:00.643 --> 10:04.545
- My life isn't over, you know.
- Okay.

10:05.048 --> 10:07.073
What doesn't kill us
makes us stronger.

10:07.550 --> 10:09.541
Well, then you must be, like, the Hulk.

10:12.622 --> 10:14.146
Let me tell you something.

10:14.357 --> 10:17.224
Chapter two of your father's story
has yet to be written.

10:18.094 --> 10:21.120
Is chapter one "I Crapped My Pants"?

10:34.511 --> 10:37.105
Is that what I think it is?

10:37.280 --> 10:41.614
- Yep, I got a prescription.
- God, I love California.

10:43.286 --> 10:46.312
Just walk into a store
and buy your weed.

10:46.489 --> 10:49.481
No more schlepping out to Reseda
and trading a piece of tail...

10:49.659 --> 10:52.093
...for a short bag of stems and seeds.

10:52.795 --> 10:54.285
You're welcome to join me here.

10:54.464 --> 10:57.661
- No, no. Not while I'm working.
- All right.

10:58.501 --> 11:00.298
Okay, I'm done working.

11:03.139 --> 11:05.630
Man, if I'd known
you liked the wacky weed...

11:05.808 --> 11:09.938
...I wouldn't have spent the last eight
years getting baked under the deck.

11:10.914 --> 11:12.711
You know, when I was on break.

11:15.318 --> 11:17.616
This is the first time
I've touched the stuff...

11:17.787 --> 11:20.620
...since a ZZ Top concert in '92.

11:20.790 --> 11:24.453
I got so paranoid I locked myself in
a Porta-Potty and tried to tunnel home.

11:26.129 --> 11:29.121
Well, good news.
Pot's a lot stronger now.

11:31.234 --> 11:32.496
What do you think?

11:34.537 --> 11:37.199
I've rolled better joints
on the back of a motorcycle...

11:37.373 --> 11:40.638
...while digging a bullet
out of my boyfriend's shoulder.

11:41.578 --> 11:45.014
All right, fine. You try it.

11:45.648 --> 11:48.082
Oh, man, I hope this helps me sleep.

11:48.251 --> 11:51.982
I can't take another night wandering
around the house thinking about Chelsea.

11:52.155 --> 11:54.020
Yeah, yeah. Boo-hoo.

11:54.190 --> 11:56.055
Let's fire up this bad boy.

12:01.998 --> 12:04.364
This is stupid.
We should've left it in the car.

12:04.534 --> 12:07.469
Well, it's very valuable, Jake.
I don't wanna see it stolen.

12:07.637 --> 12:08.661
Who steals clocks?

12:09.239 --> 12:11.605
"Clock-tomaniacs."

12:15.845 --> 12:17.676
You have your mother's
sense of humor.

12:19.249 --> 12:22.343
Okay, let's put her down real easy.

12:22.518 --> 12:24.110
Okay.

12:24.287 --> 12:26.755
Okay.

12:26.923 --> 12:27.981
Good.

12:28.157 --> 12:30.091
We have a couple of hours of daylight.

12:30.260 --> 12:32.626
How about you and I get to know
our state capital?

12:32.795 --> 12:34.786
You wanna drive to San Francisco?

12:37.066 --> 12:39.762
No, Sacramento is the capital
of California.

12:39.936 --> 12:41.767
I don't think so.

12:42.372 --> 12:44.363
Trust me. I got a map in the lobby...

12:44.540 --> 12:46.667
...that shows all the places of interest
in Old Sac.

12:46.843 --> 12:48.367
Ha, ha. Old sac. Get it?

12:48.544 --> 12:51.911
Oh, yeah.
That was much better than my joke.

12:53.249 --> 12:58.380
Look at us, a couple of nuts
hanging out in Sacramento.

13:08.831 --> 13:10.298
- Do it again.
- No. No.

13:10.466 --> 13:14.334
- Oh, come on. Please. Do it again.
- All right, all right. Last time.

13:15.505 --> 13:18.338
Badges? We don't need
no stinking badges.

13:21.144 --> 13:23.305
Okay, okay, I got one. I got one.

13:24.147 --> 13:25.512
Mm.

13:25.682 --> 13:28.014
Some folks call it a sling blade.
I call it a kaiser blade.

13:28.184 --> 13:29.879
- Mm.
- Ha-ha-ha.

13:30.620 --> 13:33.145
I like them french-fried taters. Mm.

13:33.323 --> 13:36.850
Oh, good idea.

13:37.560 --> 13:41.326
- Where you going?
- To get some of them french-fried taters.

13:41.497 --> 13:43.863
- Wait, wait, wait.
- What?

13:44.567 --> 13:46.057
I love you, Berta.

13:47.337 --> 13:49.066
I love you too, Charlie.

13:50.206 --> 13:52.071
Give me a thousand dollars.

13:54.077 --> 13:56.068
- Why?
- Well, if you have to ask...

13:56.279 --> 13:57.712
...you don't really love me.

14:00.016 --> 14:02.416
Oh, oh, and pretzels.
Get some pretzels.

14:02.585 --> 14:06.885
Pretzels?
We don't need no stinking pretzels.

14:08.925 --> 14:12.725
Oh, man, I am so lucky to have her
in my life.

14:12.895 --> 14:16.058
You've had a lot
of wonderful women in your life.

14:16.232 --> 14:19.599
But you always find a way
to sabotage the relationship.

14:20.703 --> 14:23.729
- Chelsea?
She's right, Charlie.

14:23.906 --> 14:26.238
If there's a way it can be blown,
you'll blow it.

14:26.409 --> 14:27.899
And not in the fun way.

14:28.077 --> 14:30.545
- Mia?
Tell me something, Charlie.

14:30.713 --> 14:34.274
Do you think your inability to commit
and all your macho posturing...

14:34.450 --> 14:37.214
...is because deep down
you're afraid you're gay?

14:37.387 --> 14:40.845
You know, I've wondered that too.
Are you just a big old 'mo?

14:42.024 --> 14:45.221
He's not a 'mo.
He's got mommy issues.

14:45.395 --> 14:48.728
Lots and lots of mommy issues.

14:49.399 --> 14:50.730
Lydia.

14:50.900 --> 14:53.198
Hey, it's Lydia.

14:53.369 --> 14:55.462
Excuse me.

14:55.638 --> 14:58.038
Why does everyone blame the mother?

14:58.207 --> 15:01.734
Frankly, I think you were more on target
with that homo theory.

15:02.912 --> 15:06.075
Okay. Okay, I don't wanna
be high anymore.

15:20.630 --> 15:22.598
Hey. Ask me why
they should change the name...

15:22.765 --> 15:25.131
...of the Sacramento Kings
to the Sacramento Nads.

15:25.301 --> 15:26.325
Why?

15:26.502 --> 15:30.996
That way everyone can chant,
"Go Nads! Go Nads!"

15:31.641 --> 15:33.108
Another winner.

15:33.276 --> 15:37.440
I may not be good at school or sports,
but no one beats me at ball jokes.

15:38.014 --> 15:41.609
- I'm so proud.
- Can we watch TV?

15:41.784 --> 15:44.082
We can watch TV anytime. Let's talk.

15:44.620 --> 15:47.020
You sure? That hardly ever goes well.

15:47.523 --> 15:51.254
- Come on. What's going on in your life?
- Nothing.

15:51.427 --> 15:54.021
Oh, please, you're 16.
That's a very tumultuous time.

15:54.197 --> 15:58.190
I mean, especially with all the sexual
issues and the drugs and the Internet.

15:58.401 --> 16:00.665
Yeah. You gonna eat
your chicken skin?

16:01.637 --> 16:03.434
Help yourself.

16:03.906 --> 16:07.603
- You ask me, the skin's the best part.
- Yeah, but it's not good for you.

16:07.777 --> 16:11.042
- Anyway, about your life...
- Hey, there's a business opportunity.

16:11.214 --> 16:14.775
Go to those skinless-chicken restaurants,
take the skin they throw away...

16:14.951 --> 16:18.443
...and open up a restaurant next door
named El Pollo Skin-o.

16:20.423 --> 16:23.221
That means "the chicken skin"
in Spanish.

16:24.060 --> 16:25.118
That's very clever.

16:25.294 --> 16:27.524
Guess where we'll open up
our first restaurant.

16:27.697 --> 16:29.221
Sacramento.

16:30.533 --> 16:31.557
Charming.

16:31.734 --> 16:34.965
Then Muncie, Indiana,
home of Ball State University.

16:36.072 --> 16:38.973
Then Lake Titicaca.
Not a ball joke, but still funny.

16:41.477 --> 16:43.206
Excuse me.

16:57.093 --> 16:58.151
What are you doing?

17:00.663 --> 17:02.392
Screaming into a towel.

17:03.266 --> 17:06.235
- Oh. I'm gonna watch TV.
- Okay.

17:15.678 --> 17:19.114
Oh, God, oh, God, oh, God.

17:19.282 --> 17:22.945
How many times has that been said
in this bed? Ha-ha-ha.

17:23.119 --> 17:25.280
Or in this chair.

17:25.488 --> 17:27.922
Or all over this rug.

17:29.392 --> 17:32.020
On the balcony, looking at the ocean.

17:38.100 --> 17:41.126
You're not here. You're not here.
None of you are here.

17:41.304 --> 17:43.431
Wow. So this is the bedroom.

17:44.740 --> 17:46.605
I never got past the couch.

17:46.776 --> 17:50.803
What are you complaining about?
I never got out of the car.

17:51.414 --> 17:55.908
He did me in a little church in Van Nuys.
Right in the pew.

17:57.820 --> 18:00.721
I would never let him do me
in the pew.

18:04.327 --> 18:06.261
He dumped me
when I said "I love you."

18:06.429 --> 18:09.887
He dumped me
when he saw my penis.

18:10.299 --> 18:11.891
Me too.

18:12.635 --> 18:15.900
- And he never called me again.
- Why, Charlie?

18:16.105 --> 18:17.766
Why didn't you call?

18:17.940 --> 18:19.771
Why, Charlie?

18:22.311 --> 18:25.041
I was busy. I lost your number.

18:25.581 --> 18:26.843
I was out of town.

18:27.450 --> 18:29.315
You had a penis.

18:29.485 --> 18:32.454
You, I don't know
what that thing was.

18:33.122 --> 18:36.250
Oh, God. Oh, God.

18:44.367 --> 18:47.768
This isn't happening.
This isn't happening.

18:47.937 --> 18:49.268
- Hey, Charlie.
- Aah!

18:50.706 --> 18:54.767
- Oh, Rose, not you too.
- Why not me too?

18:54.944 --> 18:57.936
Look, I am really sorry
about our one-night stand.

18:58.114 --> 19:01.948
- I know I should've called you.
- Yes, you should have.

19:02.118 --> 19:05.212
I'll tell you what,
after I come down off this stupid pot...

19:05.388 --> 19:08.118
...how about I call the real you
and take you on a date?

19:08.290 --> 19:11.123
Tell you how much you mean,
how much you've always meant.

19:11.293 --> 19:13.727
The real me would like that very much.

19:14.397 --> 19:17.491
All I could find
was donuts and chalupas.

19:17.667 --> 19:20.898
Hey, Rose.

19:24.173 --> 19:26.038
Wait, you can see her?

19:26.509 --> 19:30.639
Yeah. Why? Can't you?

19:33.382 --> 19:34.610
What the hell's going on?

19:35.351 --> 19:39.117
You're imagining Berta.

19:41.424 --> 19:42.550
Are you really here?

19:44.894 --> 19:46.987
I don't know. Am I?

19:48.531 --> 19:50.260
Call me.

19:55.371 --> 19:59.501
Okay, roll another fatty
and let's polish off these donuts.

20:09.785 --> 20:11.252
Why can't I drive?

20:11.420 --> 20:15.948
Because we are carrying a very fragile
clock that is worth a lot of money.

20:18.227 --> 20:21.094
So when you sell it,
what are you gonna do with the cash?

20:21.263 --> 20:24.755
Uh, I'm not sure. I might buy a new car.

20:24.934 --> 20:27.960
I might pay your Uncle Charlie
some of what I owe him.

20:28.170 --> 20:30.297
Uh, I might put it in your college fund.

20:32.408 --> 20:34.433
So, what kind of car
are you gonna get?

20:35.544 --> 20:38.240
- I got my eye on a Lexus convertible.
- Sweet.

20:38.414 --> 20:41.315
You know what?
That means you can have this one.

20:42.251 --> 20:43.718
No, thanks.

20:45.287 --> 20:48.586
I wanna get one of those new Camaros.
Red with yellow racing stripes.

20:48.758 --> 20:52.125
And then I'm gonna get
a big flaming skull painted on the hood.

20:52.695 --> 20:56.563
Don't you think you ought to see how
the people at Domino's feel about that?

20:58.067 --> 21:00.262
Really? You think I can get a job
at Domino's?

21:01.804 --> 21:05.934
Hey, a man's reach should exceed
his grasp, or what's a heaven for?

21:06.842 --> 21:09.436
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

21:09.612 --> 21:12.274
It means that as a human, we should...

21:12.448 --> 21:16.248
Oh, no, no, no!

21:20.523 --> 21:21.649
Now can I drive?
